{"timestamp":"2026-11-08T17:04:11.005Z","ordinal":44909,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1b054-fe0d-76c1-a45c-4726d155f0fa","turn_id":"01a1b8a7-3fc8-7460-a590-a3bb58793d59","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-de0305cf-6df1-491a-b672-fafe08bc78f8","process_id":"41866","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff -- crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/account_sync.rs crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/node_tests.rs docs/ci-maintenance.md; cat tmp/ci-critical-path/pr-body.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/ci-critical-path","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff -- crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/account_sync.rs crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/node_tests.rs docs/ci-maintenance.md; cat tmp/ci-critical-path/pr-body.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/account_sync.rs b/crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/account_sync.rs\nindex ebf7cad4..6b7a4338 100644\n--- a/crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/account_sync.rs\n+++ b/crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/account_sync.rs\n@@ -2553,26 +2553,6 @@ impl Node {\n         }\n     }\n \n-    #[cfg(test)]\n-    pub(in crate::node) async fn replay_account_history_for_test(\n-        self: &Arc<Self>,\n-        peer: &PeerRecord,\n-    ) -> Result<(), NodeError> {\n-        let mut cursor = None;\n-        loop {\n-            let (next, _, _) = self\n-                .pull_account_history_page(peer, cursor, [0; 32])\n-                .await?;\n-            let Some(next) = next else { return Ok(()) };\n-            if cursor.is_some_and(|previous| next <= previous) {\n-                return Err(NodeError::Channel(\n-                    \"fixture history replay cursor did not advance\".into(),\n-                ));\n-            }\n-            cursor = Some(next);\n-        }\n-    }\n-\n     async fn pull_account_history_page(\n         self: &Arc<Self>,\n         peer: &PeerRecord,\n@@ -2801,8 +2781,8 @@ impl Node {\n                         for (conversation, event) in offered_channels {\n                             self.trace_account_client(&peer.public, || {\n                                 format!(\n-                                    \"history_channel_committed task={:?} channel={} event={}\",\n-                                    tokio::task::try_id(),\n+                                    \"history_channel_committed revision={} channel={} event={}\",\n+                                    revision,\n                                     hex::encode(conversation),\n                                     hex::encode(event)\n                                 )\n@@ -3685,6 +3665,10 @@ impl Node {\n                                 Ok((next, digest, version)) => {\n                                     status.legacy_file_metadata = version == AccountSyncVersion::V1;\n                                     let history_complete = state.complete_page(next, digest);\n+                                    #[cfg(test)]\n+                                    if history_complete {\n+                                        self.trace_account_client(&peer.public, || format!(\"history_sweep_committed revision={revision}\"));\n+                                    }\n                                     if history_complete && !favorites_pending && !favorites_waiting { status.phase = SyncPhase::UpToDate; }\n                                     else { continuation |= !history_complete; }\n                                     if let Some(error) = &state.favorite_error {\ndiff --git a/crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/node_tests.rs b/crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/node_tests.rs\nindex fc1f6247..2da436ae 100644\n--- a/crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/node_tests.rs\n+++ b/crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/node_tests.rs\n@@ -9784,8 +9784,8 @@ async fn linked_device_catches_up_incoming_dm_after_reconnect() {\n     let delivery_work = Arc::new(Mutex::new(std::collections::BTreeMap::new()));\n     let delivery_trace_started = std::time::Instant::now();\n     let delivery_trace_omitted = Arc::new(std::sync::atomic::AtomicUsize::new(0));\n-    let replay_expected = Arc::new(Mutex::new(None::<String>));\n-    let replay_offered_erased = Arc::new(std::sync::atomic::AtomicBool::new(false));\n+    let replay_revisions = Arc::new(Mutex::new((None::<u64>, None::<u64>)));\n+    let replay_changed = Arc::new(tokio::sync::Notify::new());\n     for (label, current, peer) in [\n         (\"source\", &a1_node, a2_node.identity.public()),\n         (\"sibling\", &a2_node, a1_node.identity.public()),\n@@ -9793,15 +9793,26 @@ async fn linked_device_catches_up_incoming_dm_after_reconnect() {\n         let trace = delivery_trace.clone();\n         let work = delivery_work.clone();\n         let omitted = delivery_trace_omitted.clone();\n-        let replay_expected = replay_expected.clone();\n-        let replay_offered_erased = replay_offered_erased.clone();\n+        let replay_revisions = replay_revisions.clone();\n+        let replay_changed = replay_changed.clone();\n         *current.account_client_test_hook.lock().unwrap() =\n             Some(Arc::new(move |observed, phase| {\n-                if label == \"sibling\"\n-                    && observed == peer\n-                    && replay_expected.lock().unwrap().as_ref() == Some(&phase)\n-                {\n-                    replay_offered_erased.store(true, std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Release);\n+                if label == \"sibling\" && observed == peer {\n+                    if let Some(receipt) = phase.strip_prefix(\"history_channel_committed revision=\")\n+                        && let Some((revision, record)) = receipt.split_once(' ')\n+                        && record == format!(\"channel={} event={}\", hex::encode(channel.as_bytes()), old_channel_id.to_hex())\n+                    {\n+                        let revision: u64 = revision.parse().expect(\"owner emits a policy revision\");\n+                        let mut seen = replay_revisions.lock().unwrap();\n+                        seen.0 = Some(seen.0.map_or(revision, |old| old.max(revision)));\n+                        replay_changed.notify_one();\n+                    }\n+                    if let Some(revision) = phase.strip_prefix(\"history_sweep_committed revision=\") {\n+                        let revision: u64 = revision.parse().expect(\"owner emits a policy revision\");\n+                        let mut seen = replay_revisions.lock().unwrap();\n+                        seen.1 = Some(seen.1.map_or(revision, |old| old.max(revision)));\n+                        replay_changed.notify_one();\n+                    }\n                 }\n                 if observed != peer\n                     || !(phase.starts_with(\"dial_\")\n@@ -9988,18 +9999,30 @@ async fn linked_device_catches_up_incoming_dm_after_reconnect() {\n     }\n     new_channel_delivery.expect(\"new channel messages still arrive\");\n     phase(\"erase_recheck_begin\");\n-    // Observe an actual fresh source replay, not elapsed time or an unchanged\n-    // digest response. Keep both the real commit and query on the peer reactor.\n+    // Reset through the public policy owner: its new revision retires old\n+    // workers and clears their digest/cursor before a canonical fresh sweep.\n     let replay_node = a2_node.clone();\n-    let replay_source = a2_node.routing_peer(&a1_node.user_id()).unwrap();\n-    let expected = replay_expected.clone();\n+    let revisions = replay_revisions.clone();\n+    let changed = replay_changed.clone();\n     let permit = a2_node.runtime_work.admit().unwrap();\n     let mut replay = a2_peer.as_ref().unwrap().runtime_handle().spawn(permit.track(async move {\n-        *expected.lock().unwrap() = Some(format!(\n-            \"history_channel_committed task={:?} channel={} event={}\",\n-            tokio::task::try_id(), hex::encode(channel.as_bytes()), old_channel_id.to_hex()\n-        ));\n-        replay_node.replay_account_history_for_test(&replay_source).await?;\n+        let previous = replay_node.device_sync_policy_snapshot().1;\n+        replay_node.set_device_sync_category(crate::node::SyncCategory::History, false)?;\n+        replay_node.set_device_sync_category(crate::node::SyncCategory::History, true)?;\n+        let revision = replay_node.device_sync_policy_snapshot().1;\n+        assert!(revision > previous, \"real policy reset must advance its revision\");\n+        loop {\n+            let notified = changed.notified();\n+            tokio::pin!(notified);\n+            notified.as_mut().enable();\n+            let (offered, completed) = *revisions.lock().unwrap();\n+            if completed == Some(revision) {\n+                assert_eq!(offered, Some(revision),\n+                    \"fresh sweep must offer the exact erased payload before terminal commit\");\n+                break;\n+            }\n+            notified.await;\n+        }\n         loop {\n             match replay_node.channel_history(channel, 10) {\n                 Ok(history) => return Ok::<_, NodeError>(history),\n@@ -10009,21 +10032,26 @@ async fn linked_device_catches_up_incoming_dm_after_reconnect() {\n             tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(50)).await;\n         }\n     }));\n-    let history = match tokio::time::timeout_at(\n+    let completed = tokio::time::timeout_at(\n         new_delivery_deadline + Duration::from_secs(11), &mut replay\n-    ).await {\n+    ).await;\n+    if !matches!(&completed, Ok(Ok(Ok(_)))) {\n+        eprintln!(\"linked replay failure revisions={:?} work={:?} omitted={} phases={:?}\",\n+            replay_revisions.lock().unwrap(), delivery_work.lock().unwrap(),\n+            delivery_trace_omitted.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Relaxed),\n+            delivery_trace.lock().unwrap());\n+    }\n+    let history = match completed {\n         Ok(result) => result.expect(\"owned replay task must finish\").expect(\"linked erase replay and observation must succeed\"),\n         Err(_) => {\n-            // Cancellation does not abandon an admitted blocking commit: the\n-            // existing peer retirement below also drains its actual work owner.\n+            // Cancellation still joins the fixture task; peer retirement below\n+            // drains the coordinator's actual admitted blocking commits.\n             replay.abort();\n             let retired = replay.await;\n             assert!(retired.is_ok() || retired.is_err_and(|error| error.is_cancelled()));\n             panic!(\"linked erase replay is readable within the existing delivery and observation window\");\n         }\n     };\n-    assert!(replay_offered_erased.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Acquire),\n-        \"fresh replay must offer the exact erased channel payload and await its real commit\");\n     let history: Vec<_> = history.into_iter().filter(|entry| entry.file.is_none()).collect();\n     assert_eq!(\n         history.len(),\ndiff --git a/docs/ci-maintenance.md b/docs/ci-maintenance.md\nindex 997a9a11..d708003c 100644\n--- a/docs/ci-maintenance.md\n+++ b/docs/ci-maintenance.md\n@@ -846,6 +846,9 @@ prove the erased record was offered again and all pages were applied before\n checking that it remains absent. A successful page, unchanged-digest response or\n unrelated worker notification does not prove a complete replay. Keep deadlines\n as failure bounds, and retain ownership and joins for admitted work on timeout.\n+Request that work through its existing coordinator and observe its publication\n+revision and terminal completion. A second hand-driven page loop can race the\n+normal worker and bypass its serialization, recovery and cancellation contract.\n Give counterfactual source copies their own Cargo target directory. Relative\n package paths can collide across copies and reuse a mutated test executable;\n the canonical candidate must never consume a negative control's build output.\nThis change removes repeated CI work, consolidates chat composer and conversation actions, and adds an isolated native BLE rehearsal. All existing required checks and main-commit verification remain in place.\n\n- CI: compile each Linux/macOS workspace cohort once and execute the complete inventory through source-bound archives. Preserve native lint/build/doctest, ignored/backend, coverage and stack-symbol acceptance. Run independent work in parallel, collect on Ubuntu, keep eight serial ASan partitions with pinned tools, and remove equivalent source gates, duplicate reports and browser-install audit summaries. The explicit locked advisory gate remains.\n- Tool setup: align pinned installers across archive producers/consumers and disable source-build fallback. Fetch the pinned Gitleaks binary through the authenticated release API, bound transport attempts, verify its reviewed digest before extraction and preserve scanner failures. Full-history scanning and archive identity checks remain required.\n- Reliability: retain cancellation through log finalization and verified retirement; clean only crash-fixture-owned files; keep one automatic viewport scroll owner. Reconnect fixtures advertise a real sender listener and recover the same accepted message after a rejected handshake. The linked-device deletion check forces a fresh source replay through terminal pagination and awaited commits, proves the exact erased payload was offered, then asserts it remains absent; a fixed eleven-second wait no longer supplies readiness. The replay uses the existing node runtime and admitted-work owner under the unchanged observation deadline. Retirement-observer setup and armed admission use separate bounded phases, with a deterministic old-deadline failure control.\n- Chat: group attachments behind one accessible menu and unify conversation actions. Existing browser helpers now use the real entry point while retaining functional, permission, geometry and focus checks. Reaction summaries remain accessible without retained inline rows and in read-only views; mutation restrictions propagate into the paginated inspector, including exact search context.\n- BLE: add a bounded session byte stream, a pinned-identity encrypted-echo example and a separate macOS CoreBluetooth helper. Production discovery, node routing and wire formats are unchanged. Shutdown revokes buffered bytes; asynchronous test work is joined; the CLI confirms helper retirement before reporting success. Invalid peripheral batches are rejected atomically. This is experimental: two-host physical radio behavior is not qualified by local compilation or stream tests.\n- Maintenance: update CI/reliability guides and existing capability owners. Prefer stability and simple orchestration over arbitrary duration targets; keep squash merge as the documented default. Lifecycle fixtures supply observed private scanner dependencies while retaining real process supervision. Cheap pre-publication checks now run configured spelling over changed files (full scan when its configuration changes); the CoreBluetooth SDK spelling has a Swift-only identifier exception.\n\nLocal evidence includes the pinned-tool archive/coverage and native-symbol controls, standards/hygiene, workflow checks, 37 installer/workflow regression cases, eight Gitleaks transport/integrity/exit cases and 40 isolated validation CLI cases, the causal linked replay positive and independent no-replay negative, frontend lint/types/build, 2196 frontend tests and verified 16/16 added executable lines (100% against the unchanged 92% patch requirement) for the committed candidate. Focused chat unit tests passed; the reaction-affordance regressions failed before their fixes and then passed 12/12. Browser integration covers attachment/camera/directory races, menus, all visual-regression scenarios without snapshot updates, protection and narrow layouts, seven WebKit attachment cases, and a real-search exact-context inspector regression. The original writable paging/removal case remains intact. A separate ignored-source control that omits the real history replay fails exactly at the offered-erased-record assertion; the current implementation passes. Three real menu-selection unit cases additionally verify exactly-once callback ownership and menu closure.\n\nBLE validation passed six stream tests plus the example parser test, Swift typechecking, radio-free batch controls and helper compilation with its privacy plist. Tests on two physical Macs with IP networking disabled, permission changes, Bluetooth interruption and reconnect remain outside these results.\n\nThe complete CI run on the current commit remains required before merge, including all 33 required GitHub Actions checks and native platform acceptance. Failed or deliberately superseded attempts remain diagnostic records, not successful performance samples. Before/after measurements separate dispatch, setup, execution and runner cost; no fixed elapsed-time guarantee is claimed.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":5750}},"started_at_ms":1794157451005,"completed_at_ms":1794157451005}}
